.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SOCKETPAIR 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm socketpair
.Nd create a pair of connected sockets
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn socketpair "int domain" "int type" "int protocol" "int sv[2]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn socketpair
system call creates two unnamed local sockets connected to each other and
stores their descriptors in
.Fa sv[0]
and
.Fa sv[1] .
Either end can send and receive.
.Pp
The
.Fa domain
must be
.Dv AF_UNIX ,
the
.Fa type
one of
.Dv SOCK_STREAM ,
.Dv SOCK_DGRAM
and
.Dv SOCK_SEQPACKET ,
and the
.Fa protocol
0.
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK
may be OR'd into
.Fa type ,
as for
.Xr socket 2 ;
they apply to both descriptors.
.Pp
Each end records the creator's credentials as its peer's, for
.Xr getpeereid 3
and the options described in
.Xr unix 4 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa sv
is
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system limit on open files,
.Va kern.maxfiles ,
would be exceeded.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The
.Fa domain
is not
.Dv AF_UNIX .
.It Bq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
The
.Fa type
or
.Fa protocol
is not supported.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pipe 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn socketpair
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn socketpair
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
OxideBSD's makes real local sockets, of any of the three types; before
local sockets existed it made a pair of pipes.
